spectral-efficiency–power tradeoff. The thick envelope is the agent choice after quality gates.
mature allocation flexibility dominate the current objective. The
agent therefore preserves the conventional waveform rather than
changing for its own sake. In the terminal uplink, SC-FDMA
is selected because DFT spreading reduces PAPR99 from the
CP-OFDM region to 8.57 dB. Under the present PA model,
this yields 25.24 nJ/bit while keeping BLER at 3.78 × 10−3.
High mobility: at normalized Doppler ν = 0.30, the
OFDM-derived candidates in the current abstraction lose their
reliability and latency gates, while the OTFS delay–Doppler
representation remains feasible. OTFS provides 1.976 bit/s/Hz
at BLER 7.92 × 10−3, but its processing-complexity factor is
2.75. The selection is thus a context-dependent exchange of
compute for mobility robustness, not a universal preference
for OTFS.
Fragmented spectrum: with spectrum contiguity cf = 0.42
and a 22-dB ACLR gate, only the filtered-OFDM chain remains
spectrally feasible. Its generated waveform reaches a 22.66-dB
leakage proxy and 1.889 bit/s/Hz goodput SE. The 257-tap
Kaiser-window FIR is intentionally explicit in the candidate
manifest so that filter delay and multiply cost participate in
the decision.
Overloaded access: at offered load ρL = 1.38, orthogonal
candidates exceed their supported-load region. SCMA-over-
OFDM uses six sparse layers over four-resource groups, then
maps the superposed resources through the OFDM chain. It
is the only feasible candidate in the formal scene, reaching
2.645 bit/s/Hz aggregate goodput SE, BLER 1.06 × 10−2, and
9.92-ms P95 latency. The higher complexity factor of 4.20
remains visible and becomes decisive when the connectivity
requirement is relaxed.
The five formal operating points in Table VIII select all
five registered tools, but this one-to-one outcome is not
preprogrammed. It follows from the current gates and weights.
The continuous sweeps in Fig. 9 make that distinction testable.
CP-OFDM is selected for normalized Doppler 0–0.05, SC-
FDMA near 0.08, and OTFS from approximately 0.10 to 0.40.


